{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ivgrxvfkwx2o7ovtfttarxnzzc5sfvbjdgrw2wrtg5wozftfik7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is a trimmed `stb_ds.h` — dynamic array (`stbds_arrgrowf/arrfreef`), open-addressing hash map with binary *and* string keys and four key-ownership modes, a string arena, sip-hash/string-hash, plus the `strkey`/`sh_puts` helpers. 16 exported symbols.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all mechanically derived)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` surface; **16 C exports → 16 Rust exports, diff empty**; 0 unresolved non-libc imports. Also the build-config enumeration: Cargo.toml has **no `[features]`** and CMakeLists has no `option()`/`#if*`, so there is exactly **one** configuration (default ≡ `--no-default-features` ≡ `--all-features`, all `cargo check`ed) |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **42 rows**, one per distinct C rejection site (every early return, every `STBDS_ASSERT`, every unchecked deref, out-of-range enums, zero/oversized lengths) — 0 unchecked |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **53 rows** — the pruned cross-product of `mode` × table `string.mode` × table lifecycle × bucket-probe half × `elemsize`/`keysize`/`keyoffset` × arena shape × seed × data shape — 0 unchecked |\n\n## Phases B–D — 95 differential tests\nBoth `.so`s are `dlopen`ed via `libloading`; **no Rust function is ever called directly**. The macro layer (`hmput`, `shput`, `shputs`, `hmgeti_ts`, `hmdel`, `hmdefault`, `arrput`, `sh_new_arena`…) is spelled out so the low-level entry points are driven directly. After **every** operation the two maps are deep-compared: array header, the whole `stbds_hash_index`, **every bucket's `hash[8]`/`index[8]`**, every raw element byte, arena `block`/`remaining` trace, storage alignment. Inputs are fixed-seed randomized. Crashes are compared by `fork()`ing per library and comparing signal *and stderr*; `sh_puts` by `dup2` stdout capture. `hashmap.rs::table_lifecycle_coverage` proves growth, shrink, tombstone rebuild and tombstone reuse are all actually exercised.\n\n## Three real translation defects found and fixed (C never touched)\n1. **`stbds_stralloc`**: `512u << (a->block >> 1)` — `a->block` is `unsigned char`, so the shift count reaches 127. gcc emits `shl` (masks `& 63`); Rust `<<` is an overflow error → **panicked in debug builds**. Fixed with `wrapping_shl`; now swept over all 256 `block` values.\n2. **`STBDS_ROTATE_*` / sip-hash block counter**: plain `<<`/`>>`/`+` → converted to `wrapping_*`.\n3. **`STBDS_ASSERT` message text**: the C's `assert` embeds `__FILE__` as an *absolute* path; the translation hard-coded `\"src/lib.c\"`. Added `build.rs` to canonicalize `c_src/src/lib.c`. `errors.rs::e23_hmdel_keyoffset_abort` reaches a genuinely reachable assertion (`hmdel_key` with `keyoffset != 0`) and both libraries now emit byte-identical stderr.\n\nTwo of my own test bugs were also fixed (comparing `realloc` pointer-identity across two heaps; a null-map deref).\n\n## Documented non-divergences (in `ERRORS.md`)\n- Rust's `debug` profile UB-checks convert the C's null-deref `SIGSEGV` into `SIGABRT`; **release** (the shipped artifact) matches exactly.\n- `hmdel_key` with `mode >= 2` + a `memmove` fix-up hashes raw pointer bytes as text, so it's heap-address-dependent even for the C against itself; pinned down deterministically via `SH_DEFAULT` (caller-owned key pointers).\n\n`./verify.sh` re-runs the whole matrix: **95 tests × 3 feature combinations × 2 build profiles, symbol diff empty — ALL PASSED.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1140,"cache_read_input_tokens":301854,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1140,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2081d